    "description": "Finds cancer cell lines by what they carry and what they lack: a gene, a protein change or a mutation class (KRAS G12C, EGFR exon 19 deletions), genes with no mutation called (for example TP53 or STK11 wild-type), and a cancer type, across 1,893 cancer cell lines and 209 cancer genes from DepMap Public 26Q3 and the Cancer Cell Line Encyclopedia, with Cellosaurus names. Each result links the line's page (its driver mutations, copy number, expression and identity), and the list downloads as CSV. Free, no account; DepMap's terms of use apply to the data.",
